
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I&#8217;m late linking this one, but it&#8217;s worth catching up on. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uQ3lL68hNK4">Joanna Stern spent a week with the new Siri</a> in iOS 27, and her verdict is that it&#8217;s very good.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Her take matches mine. The new Siri pulls context from Messages, Calendar, and the rest of your iPhone life, and it answers questions the old Siri would have flubbed. It&#8217;s solid. After a decade of Siri letdowns, it&#8217;s nice to write that sentence.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It&#8217;s not the most powerful AI on my devices. The things I do with Claude and a stack of MCPs run circles around anything Siri can pull off. That&#8217;s a high bar though, and it misses the point. Siri is finally part of the AI conversation at all. That&#8217;s new.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">What I want now is for third-party developers to build for it. Siri gets a lot more interesting the moment my apps can hand it real work. If developers get behind it, the version Joanna reviewed is just the floor.</p>
